+
+## Changed files and remaining acceptance
+
+`game/track/native_track_visual.gd` (kit version, bounded scenery); `game/track/surface_detail.gdshaderinc` (dune/shoulder pigment and relief); `game/track/track_theme.gd` (desert palette/daylight); `game/vehicle/skid_trails.gd` (isolated corrected sand grooves); new `game/tests/capture_desert_style.gd` and UID; this report, evidence, `DEVELOPMENT_STATUS.md` and `docs/PHASE_0_PLAN.md`.
+
+The scoped Git checkpoint is `docs/evidence/desert-hierarchy-2026-10-03/desert-hierarchy.patch`, containing these runtime/capture files and the report. Shared status files, screenshots and unrelated concurrent work are excluded from the patch. No mixed-workspace commit was made.
+
+Owner review of the revised objects/colors and tire marks, driving-camera motion at all joins, creator refresh/undo on representative tracks, sustained phone/GPU/thermal cost of cover, and device readability remain to be checked. Existing running race scenery must be rebuilt by starting a new race/restarting the game to display the revised meshes. The pre-existing creator-New failures remain unresolved. Full replay/regression validation was not rerun because this task changes presentation only; no full-suite pass is claimed.
